    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0220" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1694.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President of China to the
                            President of the United States.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-05-02">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 2, 1913</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the name of the Republic of China I thank you most heartily for the message of
                    recognition which you have sent to me through your honored representative in
                    this capital. The sentiments of amity and good will which it bespeaks and the
                    expressions of greeting and welcome which it conveys at once testify to the
                    American spirit of mutual helpfulness and adds another brilliant page to the
                    history of 70 years of uninterrupted friendly intercourse between China and the
                    United States. Though unfamiliar with the republican form of government the
                    Chinese people are yet fully convinced of the soundness of the principle which
                    underlies it and which is so luminously represented by your glorious
                    Commonwealth. The sole aim of the Government which they have established,
                    therefore, is and will be to preserve this form of government and to perfect its
                    workings to the end that they may enjoy its unalloyed blessings, prosperity, and
                    happiness within, through union of law and liberty, and peace and friendship
                    without, through the faithful execution of all established obligations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Yuan Shih-kai</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">President of the Republic of China</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
